+
+  <p class="note-line">
+    Official pages worth checking before you apply: <a href="https://iimcat.ac.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CAT (IIM)</a>, <a href="https://exams.nta.nic.in/cuet-pg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CUET PG (NTA)</a>, <a href="https://web.ncte.gov.in/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCTE</a> and <a href="https://iimc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IIMC</a>. For the ranked ROI view of courses, read <a href="/blog/college-degrees/best-courses-after-ba-for-good-salary-india/">best courses after BA for good salary</a>.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2 id="exam">Lane 3: the exam lane and its real odds</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    Exams give the most stable outcome in India and the lowest odds per attempt. You can only decide sensibly with the numbers in front of you.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="table-wrap">
+    <table class="paths-table">
+      <thead>
+        <tr>
+          <th>Exam</th>
+          <th>The numbers</th>
+          <th>What it means</th>
+        </tr>
+      </thead>
+      <tbody>
+        {oddsRows.map((row) => (
+          <tr>
+            <td data-label="Exam"><strong>{row.exam}</strong></td>
+            <td data-label="The numbers">{row.numbers}</td>
+            <td data-label="What it means">{row.reading}</td>
+          </tr>
+        ))}
+      </tbody>
+    </table>
+  </div>
+
+  <p class="note-line">
+    Sources: <a href="https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2235933&reg=3&lang=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PIB summary of the UPSC CSE 2025 result</a>, and the notices on <a href="https://ssc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSC</a>, <a href="https://www.ibps.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBPS</a> and <a href="https://upsc.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UPSC</a>. Vacancy counts get revised, so verify on the official notice before you plan.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="honest-take">
+    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take: two stages of competition</p>
+    <p>
+      Getting in is the first filter. UPSC alone has a prelims, a mains and an interview. Even after selection, service allocation and posting are ranked again. Clearing one round does not shrink the next.
+    </p>
+    <p>
+      Arts graduates are not at a disadvantage here. Humanities graduates were about 29% of selected candidates in 2023-24, and 84.1% of optional subjects chosen by selected candidates were humanities, per <a href="https://theprint.in/feature/engineers-53-per-cent-upsc-selections/2927230/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ThePrint's reading of the UPSC report</a>. The subject helps; the base rate still stands.
+    </p>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
+    <p>
+      <strong>Run the exam with an income:</strong> you can prepare for SSC CGL or bank exams while working, and it keeps a safety net under you. Read <a href="/blog/government-jobs/government-exam-preparation-while-working-india/">how to prepare while working</a> and <a href="/blog/government-jobs/ssc-vs-bank-exams-which-to-prepare-india/">SSC vs bank exams</a> before choosing.
+    </p>
+  </div>
+
+  <p class="note-line">
+    If an attempt does not work out, <a href="/blog/government-jobs/what-to-do-after-failed-upsc-attempts-india/">what to do after failed UPSC attempts</a> and <a href="/blog/career-options/upsc-alternative-careers-for-humanities-students-india/">UPSC alternative careers for humanities students</a> map the next moves.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2 id="subject-map">Which lane your BA subject feeds</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    Your subject does shape which doors open faster. Use this as a starting map, then check the syllabus and eligibility yourself.
+  </p>
+
