+
+  <h2 id="checkpoint">Use The 4-Checkpoint Protocol on every row you shortlist</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    The 4-Checkpoint Protocol cuts through the pressure at home and online. Run each of your three chosen rows through it.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="protocol-stack">
+    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
+      <div class="checkpoint">
+        <div class="checkpoint__num">{item.num}</div>
+        <div class="checkpoint__body">
+          <div class="checkpoint__title">{item.title}</div>
+          <p>{item.body}</p>
+          <div class="checkpoint__note">{item.note}</div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    ))}
+  </div>
+
+  <h2 id="gates">Pass The 3 Gates before you pay for years</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    The 4-Checkpoint Protocol compares routes on paper. The 3 Gates test them in real life.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="gates-block">
+    <p class="gates-block__title">Pass all three before you commit a large sum or a long stretch of time.</p>
+    <div class="gates-row">
+      {gateItems.map((item) => (
+        <div class="gate">
+          <span class="gate__num">{item.num}</span>
+          <span class="gate__name">{item.title}</span>
+          <p>{item.body}</p>
+        </div>
+      ))}
+    </div>
+  </div>
+
+  <h2 id="skills">Add the skill layer that raises your ceiling</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    Two students in the same row can earn very different amounts. The difference is usually a skill portfolio: one core skill, one multiplier skill and visible proof.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="feature-grid">
+    <div class="feature-card">
+      <div class="feature-card__label">Core skill</div>
+      <div class="feature-card__title">What the row trains you to do</div>
+      <p>Coding for B.Tech and BCA, accounting and analysis for commerce, drafting for law, drawing and problem framing for design.</p>
+    </div>
+    <div class="feature-card">
+      <div class="feature-card__label">Multiplier skill</div>
+      <div class="feature-card__title">What makes the core skill pay more</div>
+      <p>Clear English, spreadsheet and data reading, sales sense, or the ability to use AI tools well and check their output. Regional-medium students can build English steadily through short daily practice; it is a trainable skill, not a talent.</p>
+    </div>
+    <div class="feature-card">
+      <div class="feature-card__label">Proof</div>
+      <div class="feature-card__title">What another person can see</div>
+      <p>A deployed project, a financial model, a case note, a design sample or a short explainer video. One finished piece beats five unfinished intentions.</p>
+    </div>
+    <div class="feature-card">
+      <div class="feature-card__label">AI layer</div>
+      <div class="feature-card__title">Start now, deepen later</div>
+      <p>Begin by using AI to research, draft and check your own work while you study. Later, learn to build small automations inside your field. Routine data entry and template work are the most exposed; judgement and licensed practice are not.</p>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
+    <p>Some rows scale beyond a salary. A CA or law practice, a design studio, a coaching or online teaching business, and a small clinic or lab-services business are owned paths.</p>
+    <p>They scale because you set the price and can add people or reach beyond your own hours, but each takes years of proof and client trust, so treat them as a later step.</p>
+  </div>
+
+  <h2 id="money">The money check every row must pass</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    College is one part of your total education budget, not the whole of it. As a strict planning heuristic, not a fact of nature, keep college spending near 10% of the complete education budget when you can. If the budget is ₹10 lakh, start from about ₹1 lakh for college and keep the rest for tools, books, projects, current online learning and the years before your income stabilises.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="honest-take">
+    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
+    <p>Going well above that needs a reason you can name. Examples are a licence you cannot get otherwise, laboratory or clinical access, or verified placement outcomes at that particular college for that particular course.</p>
+    <p>Avoid taking a large loan for a degree whose first-year pay is in the ₹2 to 4 lakh range. Loans suit only routes where the credential is required and the outcome is verified.</p>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    Free and low-cost learning through YouTube, official documentation and reputable online platforms is often more current than a college syllabus for digital fields. It does not replace an accredited degree, licence or clinical training where the law demands one.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2 id="misreads">Five ways students misread a career chart</h2>
+
