+>
+  <p class="lead-para">
+    <strong>Career options after 12th are best chosen by lane, not by stream label.</strong>
+    Pick the lane that fits how you work, what your family can afford, and what you can prove, because a high-income skill portfolio built early opens more choices and a faster route to financial freedom than a famous course name.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="key-takeaways">
+    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li>There are six real lanes after 12th: build and ship, business and finance, licensed professions, words and media, public service, and earn-while-you-learn.</li>
+      <li>Run each lane through the 4-Checkpoint Protocol (your energy, life context, market demand, AI risk) and pass The 3 Gates of proof before you spend big money.</li>
+      <li>Next step: shortlist two lanes, talk to one working person in each, and run a small real test before the admission deadline.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    Most students do not lack options after 12th. They lack a map that shows the seat math, the real deadlines, and the cost of a wrong turn.
+  </p>
+
+  <p>
