+
+  <h2 id="salary">How to read a salary claim before you trust it</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    Fresher pay differs a lot by college tier, city, employer type, and role, so a single number in an article is close to meaningless. Instead of hunting for a "best salary", test any claim with these questions.
+  </p>
+
+  <ol class="rich-list">
+    <li><strong>Is it median or top?</strong> A top package describes one student. The median describes the middle of the class.</li>
+    <li><strong>How many students does it count?</strong> A placement report that covers only placed students hides everyone who did not get an offer.</li>
+    <li><strong>What stage is it?</strong> Starting pay, year five, and senior pay are three different numbers.</li>
+    <li><strong>Which employer type?</strong> A product company, a service company, a start-up, a government body, and a family firm pay differently.</li>
+    <li><strong>What did it cost to get there?</strong> Subtract fees, loan interest, and years without income before you call a path "high paying".</li>
+  </ol>
+
+  <p class="note-line">
+    For earn-while-you-learn routes there is an official floor: the revised NATS minimum stipend from 1 April 2026 is ₹9,600 for vocational technician apprentices, ₹10,900 for diploma holders, and ₹12,300 for graduates. Employers can pay more.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2 id="doors">Exit points, credits, and two degrees: keep the doors open</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    You are not locked in at admission. Under the UGC framework linked to NEP 2020, a four-year undergraduate programme lets you exit with a certificate after one year, a diploma after two, a bachelor's degree after three, or an honours or research degree after four. Credits can be stored in the Academic Bank of Credits, and students can generally resume within a set window.
+  </p>
+
+  <p>
+    UGC guidelines from April 2022 also allow two degrees at the same time (physical plus online, for example), as long as class schedules do not overlap. Universities may still raise paperwork issues, so ask the admissions office before you plan on it.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="honest-take">
+    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
+    <p>
+      "Keep options open" is useful only when it is cheap. A second degree, a repeat year, or an expensive course used only to delay a decision is not keeping options open. It is paying to postpone.
+    </p>
+  </div>
