+>
+  <p class="lead-para">
+    <strong>Career options in commerce without maths are wider than most families think, because only a short list of degrees and exams checks for a maths subject on your marksheet.</strong>
+    CA, most BBA programmes, bank PO, law, marketing, HR and accounting practice stay open. What closes is narrow and specific, and this guide names it so you can build a high-income skill portfolio without guessing.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="key-takeaways">
+    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Answer: a few gates close, such as DU's BA (Hons) Economics, BMS and BBA (FIA), IIM Amritsar's IPM, and engineering entrances. CA, CFA enrolment, bank PO, B.Com (Hons) at DU through Accountancy, and law do not ask for Class 12 maths.</li>
+      <li>Decision filter: ask whether the "maths" is a Class 12 subject on the eligibility page, or a timed section you can practise. The first is a wall, the second is a training problem.</li>
+      <li><strong>Next step: shortlist two paths, check the official eligibility line for each, and build one piece of proof. That is how a skill portfolio turns into higher income and earlier financial freedom.</strong></li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    This page is about one specific worry: a missing maths subject. If you want the full role-by-role map of commerce work, read <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-in-commerce/">career options in commerce</a>. For the wider after-school picture, see <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-after-12th-commerce/">career options after 12th commerce</a>. For degree and course fees, use <a href="/blog/college-degrees/courses-for-commerce-students-after-12th/">courses for commerce students after 12th</a>.
+  </p>
+
+  <p>
+    What is different here: those pages ask what you want to do. This one asks what your marksheet allows and what needs practice. More guides like it sit in <a href="/blog/career-options/">career options</a>. If you are stuck between paths, <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">continuous career guidance</a> helps you choose the skill mix and proof that fits you, and the <a href="/career-skills-compass/">Career &amp; Skills Compass</a> helps you read your strengths first.
+  </p>
