+  <p class="lead-para">
+    <strong>MBA career options in India come down to nine lanes, and your institute decides which of them are open on day one.</strong>
+    At the top institutes almost every lane is available, from consulting to product to finance. Below that, the
+    doors narrow to BFSI, sales, operations, and HR, and the real growth comes from a second job and a skill layer
+    you build yourself. Picking the lane before the fee form is how you protect lakhs of rupees, and pairing the
+    degree with a high-income skill portfolio is what creates better options and earlier financial freedom.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="key-takeaways">
+    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Consulting, product, and finance pay the most, but at entry they are mostly top-institute doors. IIM Calcutta 2026 averaged Rs 36 LPA; some IIMs averaged far less.</li>
+      <li>Sales, relationship, operations, and HR roles hire in the largest numbers and are where most graduates start.</li>
+      <li>Regulator roles like RBI Grade B and SEBI Grade A are exam routes, and RBI Grade B does not require an MBA.</li>
+      <li><strong>Pick a lane by weekly work, your institute's real recruiter list, and the proof you can show, then plan the second job.</strong></li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    Role lists are everywhere. The harder decision behind them is which door to walk through, and you will find more like it in
+    our <a href="/blog/career-options/">career options library</a>. If you are weighing a degree fee against a
+    specific lane and want a plan you can show your family,
+    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
+    helps you compare lanes, proof, and money before you commit.
+  </p>
