+
+  <h2 id="neet-shift">Why "without NEET" is getting narrower</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    Many guides, videos and forum answers still say nursing and physiotherapy need no NEET. That was mostly true. It is now changing.
+  </p>
+
+  <p>
+    Andhra Pradesh moved its four-year BSc Nursing admission to NEET UG from 2026-27, covering government and private colleges, in place of the earlier state test. Separately, the National Commission for Allied and Healthcare Professions asked UGC to make NEET appearance a requirement for BPT and BOT from 2026-27, with no minimum marks. That proposal applies only where states and universities adopt it, and Karnataka, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu and Gujarat were reported as agreeing.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="callout callout--amber">
+    <p class="callout__eyebrow">What this means for you</p>
+    <ul class="callout__list">
+      <li>Sit NEET even if MBBS is not your goal. Appearing keeps nursing, physiotherapy, occupational therapy, AYUSH and veterinary counselling open.</li>
+      <li>Ask each college which route applies to your state and year. Do not rely on last year's answer.</li>
+      <li>Colleges that promise admission "without any exam" for regulated courses deserve extra checking of their approvals.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    The NCAHP Act itself groups allied and healthcare work into ten broad categories, including medical laboratory sciences, physiotherapy, nutrition, ophthalmic sciences, occupational therapy, radiology and imaging, and health information management. That breadth is why allied health is a real career lane and not a consolation prize.
+  </p>
+
