+  <h2 id="still-choosing">If you are still choosing PCB</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    If you are in Class 10 or early Class 11 and PCB is only one option, be strict with yourself. Choose it if you genuinely like biology and healthcare or life-science work, understand how long the training paths run, and have realistic backups.
+  </p>
+
+  <p>
+    If you are undecided and can handle Mathematics, PCM is the broader default because it keeps technology, data and many degrees open, though it closes medicine and some agriculture and life-science routes. Neither stream is universal. Decide by interest, ability, eligibility, cost, time to income and the skills you can build alongside.
+  </p>
