+>
+  <p class="lead-para">
+    <strong>The best certificate courses for BCom students are the ones a stranger can verify: a NISM exam for markets and wealth roles, the GST practitioner route for tax work, a TallyPrime certificate for accounts, and Power BI for reporting roles.</strong>
+    A certificate an employer cannot check is only a receipt. Pick the few that carry weight, prove them
+    with one piece of real work, and your BCom starts building a high-income skill portfolio, which is
+    what opens better income opportunities and moves you toward earlier financial freedom.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="key-takeaways">
+    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Rank certificates by who issues them, not by how long the syllabus is. Exam bodies and software makers beat private institutes.</li>
+      <li>Cheap and real: NISM exams at Rs 1,500, a free SEBI Investor Awareness Test, and free SWAYAM courses that may count for college credit.</li>
+      <li>Fees for the same subject differ by 3 to 6 times between institutes. Compare before you pay.</li>
+      <li>Next step: choose one lane (accounts, markets, or analysis), take one certificate, and build one project with it.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
