+
+  <div class="honest-take">
+    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
+    <p>
+      A degree still matters: many jobs and professional routes need it, and the BCom itself is what makes
+      you eligible for things like GST practitioner enrolment. The trap is degree-only thinking. A BCom
+      with one verified certificate and one finished project beats a BCom with six course papers.
+    </p>
+  </div>
+
+  <h2 id="rung-1">Rung 1: exam-body certificates (NISM and GST practitioner)</h2>
+
+  <p>
+    NISM, the National Institute of Securities Markets, runs certification exams for the securities
+    industry. The exams are online and remote-proctored, and most certificates stay valid for about 3
+    years. NISM's own FAQ for the Equity Derivatives exam says it is open to students, not only to people
+    already working in broking. Study material can be downloaded from NISM for free.
+  </p>
