+>
+  <p class="lead-para">
+    <strong>The career development skills worth building are the ones that remove what is blocking you
+    right now, not the ten on a generic list.</strong> If you are not getting shortlisted, you need
+    visible proof in one role. If you get interviews but no offers, you need to explain real work. If you
+    are employed but stuck, you need a skill that widens your scope. If your pay is capped, you need a
+    multiplier. Choose one, prove it, and you are building a high-income skill portfolio instead of a
+    longer CV.
+  </p>
+
+  <div class="key-takeaways">
+    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Career development skills are not one list. The right one depends on your blocker: no shortlists, no offers, no growth, or a pay ceiling.</li>
+      <li>Build one core skill, add one multiplier, and keep the human layer (judgment, trust, explanation) that AI does not replace easily.</li>
+      <li><strong>A skill only counts once someone else can see it. A finished sample or a documented result unlocks high-income opportunities faster than another certificate.</strong></li>
+      <li>Start with free and low-cost routes, and pay only for feedback or structure that free material cannot give you. Next step: name your blocker below, then pick one skill to test.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <p>
+    This sits inside the wider <a href="/blog/skills/">Skills section</a>. If you want a person to look at
+    your situation and pick the right skill with you, see
+    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
+    built around a skill portfolio and earlier financial freedom.
+  </p>
+
+  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
